Description: Executes the distributed OHDSI network study pipeline for large-scale
  clinical concept association mining (Concept AB Mining Engine v57). All SQL algorithms,
  database architectures, random partitioning logic, continuity-corrected directionality
  formulations, and original analytic code were conceived and authored by Stephen H. Bandeian,
  MD, JD (Principal Investigator, Johns Hopkins University). Computes encounter-level and
  population-level co-occurrence statistics across OMOP CDM standard clinical domains
  (Condition, Drug, Measurement, Procedure, Device, Observation) partitioned into random batches
  to optimize memory and disk utilization. Evaluates temporal precedence, crude and healthcare
  utilization-stratified lift, odds ratios, and continuity-corrected directionality ratios
  with complete privacy preservation and zero patient-level data export.
